Init: every engine with a persist entry runs one chunk in its persistent state before the
makefiles are read. The chunk comes from AMK_<NAME>_INIT, a chunk or an @path, else from
the payload's __init__.<name>; a payload without one is the normal case and says nothing,
a named path that cannot be read says so. Output goes to stderr. A zygote runs it once
and every request inherits the result, and a hook the chunk registers is in place for the
first goals event, so a distribution's guest-side code is loaded where the parse lives.

--- a/src/amk.h
+++ b/src/amk.h
@@ -35,4 +35,5 @@
 void amk_forget_children (void);
 void amk_hook_fire (enum amk_event event, const struct amk_event_info *info);
+void amk_engine_init (void);
-
+
 extern int gawk_main (int argc, char **argv);
--- a/src/function.c
+++ b/src/function.c
@@ -2542,4 +2542,69 @@
       e->hook (amk_event_names[event], info->target, info->status, info->exit_code, info->exit_sig, (long) info->pid);
 }
